# CONFIG - Configure startup and disk bindings

```text
CONFIG
CONFIG /SHOW
```

## Inspect settings

/SHOW displays the configuration. Run CONFIG without an argument to
enter its menus. A logical drive binding associates a CP/M letter with a
physical drive and a disk format. Match the format to the mounted media
before accessing it.

## Cold startup

```text
CONFIG /STARTUP="SUBMIT STARTUP"
```

This selects A0:STARTUP.SUB as the command procedure for cold boot. Edit
its commands with a text editor. Use CONFIG's save menu to write the
settings for a subsequent cold boot. See [SUBMIT](SUBMIT.HLP) for
command-file syntax.

## Bind a drive

```text
CONFIG /LOGICAL=D /PHYSICAL=3 /FORMAT="DRI 8-inch CP/M Standard 77T SS"
```

The example binds D to physical unit 3. Use the exact format name from
your catalogue and the physical unit for your machine.
